BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 662.0 Tm (first sector boundary. It records block counts, free counts, inode counts, block size,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 645.0 Tm (per-group geometry, compatible/incompatible/readonly-compatible feature flags and volume) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 628.0 Tm (state. Block group descriptors locate their bitmaps and inode tables; backups of important) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 611.0 Tm (metadata are placed according to revision and sparse-super rules.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 582.0 Tm (Each inode records file mode, ownership, timestamps, link count, size and block references.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 565.0 Tm (Traditional ext2 block pointers use direct, single-indirect, double-indirect and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 548.0 Tm (triple-indirect addressing, allowing progressively larger files. The inode data mapping is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 531.0 Tm (separate from the directory that names the file. Correct interpretation requires matching) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 514.0 Tm (inode size, directory entry revision and enabled feature flags.) Tj ET
