BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 679.0 Tm (The original ext2 format has no metadata journal. A crash during allocation or directory) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 662.0 Tm (modification can leave mismatches among bitmaps, inode pointers, link counts and directory) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 645.0 Tm (entries. The superblock records clean/dirty or error state, and e2fsck can perform a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 628.0 Tm (structured scan of allocation, namespace and connectivity to restore consistency when) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 611.0 Tm (evidence permits.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 582.0 Tm (Recovery cannot assume bitmap truth, because the bitmap may have been updated before a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 565.0 Tm (related inode pointer. An offline checker cross-correlates group descriptors, metadata) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 548.0 Tm (reservations, block maps, inode ownership and directory reachability. Feature flags prevent) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 531.0 Tm (old implementations from writing to formats they do not safely understand. A copied) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.15 Tf 0.08 0.15 0.24 rg 1 0 0 1 50 514.0 Tm (superblock alone does not establish that all file content survived.) Tj ET
